{"lens":{"fp":"2997338152-24561","payload":"{\"score\":9,\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh\",\"category\":\"startup cost\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"plugin.sh runs a `$(cd ...)` subshell at load time to locate claim.sh, a fork the design decision document explicitly said to avoid by not having plugin.sh source claim.sh at all.\",\"quote\":\"_ccgl_plugin_dir=\\\"$(cd \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}\\\" 2>/dev/null || true; pwd)\\\"\",\"trigger\":\"Every time plugin.sh is loaded for the first time in a process (guarded by `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_GH_LABELS_LOADED`, so once per runner process). The design doc for this issue states: 'plugin.sh must not source core/claim/claim.sh — that would create a circular dependency and add a startup $(cd ...) subshell in plugin.sh's load path.' The code does exactly what the design said not to do.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"},{\"file\":\"core/claim/claim.sh\",\"category\":\"unnecessary subshell\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"`_ccgl_read_holder` calls `$(_ccgl_backend)` — a subshell that only echoes a variable — while the other new functions in claim.sh (`_zbuild_claim_read_labels_into`, `_zbuild_claim_add_label_direct`) explicitly replaced the same pattern with `${ZBUILD_CLAIM_BACKEND:-gh}` to avoid the fork.\",\"quote\":\"case \\\"$(_ccgl_backend)\\\" in\",\"trigger\":\"When `zbuild:claimed` is already on the issue and `zbuild_claim_acquire` calls `_ccgl_read_holder` on the conflict path; not in a hot loop, but the inconsistency is introduced here while the design comments in the same file call it out as avoided elsewhere.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"}]}","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"2e2649a7ef6be6c9ab172921cc93401399968c6a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"9c5e4918b9c2dd16c79aecbdd522a427e77449b0"}},"scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh":{"fp":"942004488-25604:file:scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh","payload":"clean: no finding\n[]","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/registry.sh":"3a46f76258dd2ab5d9b9288827f822cecffc56fc","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/discovery.sh":"127a064695f20869e15e14d04224342c02a489fb","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/manifest-validation.sh":"ea99ff5027262df80fc30430bb4714c790250770","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"70e7aca83387ee35ec149c1cdf06100c46f089f8","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/lifecycle.sh":"c8332c60cf55775cf63ad0ecb99492b095eb5855","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/scripts/lib/run-status-render.sh":"e66946ae97fcf967c5f77ee2ea2518de3b7fda3b"},"base":{"head":"3300f9f9aacc51ab294412f0f003c7692c1f3ce0","files":{}}},"core/claim/claim.sh":{"fp":"942004488-25604:file:core/claim/claim.sh","payload":"found: findings\n[{\"file\":\"core/claim/claim.sh\",\"category\":\"redundant subprocess\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"message\":\"`_zbuild_claim_find_coordinator_v` calls `discover_plugins` inside a process substitution, so the in-shell discovery cache (`_ZBUILD_DISCOVERY_CACHE`) filled inside it dies with the subshell; the function is called twice per issue-bound run (once in `zbuild_claim_acquire` and once in `zbuild_claim_release`), so each call falls through to the file memo path, which requires a `find` for the shape check on every invocation rather than once.\",\"quote\":\"done < <(discover_plugins \\\"$_search_root\\\" 2>/dev/null || true)\",\"trigger\":\"Every issue-bound run calls `_zbuild_claim_find_coordinator_v` twice — once at acquire and once at release; each call forks a subshell for `discover_plugins`, loses the in-shell cache, and executes a `find` for the shape check to reach the file memo, where `discover_plugins_into` would populate `_ZBUILD_DISCOVERY_CACHE` in the caller's shell and let the second call skip that `find` entirely.\",\"accepted_if\":\"The coordinator lookup on each of the two calls (acquire and release) does not fork a subshell for discovery, so the in-shell discovery cache populated on the first call is available to the second call without an additional filesystem shape check.\",\"introduced\":true,\"fix\":\"code\"}]","files":{"/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/registry.sh":"3a46f76258dd2ab5d9b9288827f822cecffc56fc","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/discovery.sh":"127a064695f20869e15e14d04224342c02a489fb","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/manifest-validation.sh":"ea99ff5027262df80fc30430bb4714c790250770","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh":"70e7aca83387ee35ec149c1cdf06100c46f089f8","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/plugin-registry/lifecycle.sh":"c8332c60cf55775cf63ad0ecb99492b095eb5855","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/config/adr-enforcement-baseline.txt":"8f959db802864d3711fb73f512a6d2aa24c4859d","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/config/event-schema.json":"30dce672627cb047400df8eb0e095c14e8917247","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/claim/claim.sh":"707f8ea05518fe3845c2d8ef7b8912a5c2f36ccd","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/core/pipeline/runner.sh":"640b4c0571bfe697f236a515f95be55b18d805f9","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/docs/adr/ADR-005-claim-coordinator.md":"cb484550d5797621e2427cc2e122c3ba49b4697a","/home/runner/.zbuild/repos/ezigus/zBuild/issues/1764/worktree/docs/adr/AD